  "result": "I wrote the 10-minute lesson on O3 at `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`. I haven't opened it in a browser or run a word count, so the length is an estimate from my section plan.\n\nIt teaches three concepts, each with a worked trace from the makerspace assistant, then the name, a \"Why this works\" box and a check question:\n1. **The context window.** Within a run, the program re-sends the whole growing message list on every model call, so each token kept in context is paid for again.\n2. **Notes as memory between sessions.** A new session starts with an empty window, so only facts saved outside it, such as a per-student notes file, survive.\n3. **Retrieval.** The assistant pulls in only the manual section it needs, instead of loading the whole manual.\n\nThe lesson also has a warm-up on the agent loop, a figure, a misconception box (\"a bigger window means it remembers students\"), a worked example with a faded task, and a summary. It doesn't reuse any quiz item or give away a quiz answer.\n\nI also created `RESOURCES.md` with the two sources the lesson cites: Anthropic's context-engineering post and the memory tool docs. I added a line to `NOTES.md` recording what the lesson covered and left out: compaction, and how retrieval search finds a page.\n\nThe lesson is 10 minutes because you asked for that. Ask for a shorter or longer one if you'd like. When you're ready, ask for a quiz on it, or ask me anything about it.\n\nQuestion for you: do you want the next session to cover how retrieval search finds the right page, or compaction (what to do when the window fills mid-run)?",
